{"title": "Components/Checkbox/Checkbox Group", "docs": {"text": "CheckboxGroup\nAccessible AA\nWeb\nAndroid\niOS\nFlutter\nCMP\nExample Checkbox Group\n\nOption 1\n\nOption 2\n\nOption 3\n\nOption 4\nShow code\nCopy code\nODSCheckboxGroup extends the ODSCheckbox as well as the native HTMLInputElement properties as React props. On top of the additional properties that are listed below, you can also pass the native HTMLInputElement properties as React props. You can read more about those properties here.\n\n\nName\tDescription\tDefault\tControl\ncheckboxProps\t\nThe Checkbox props. If the type is standard, this property will be ignored.\nOmit<ODSCheckboxProps, \"aria-checked\" | \"onChange\" | \"size\" | \"checked\" | \"indeterminate\" | \"disabled\" | \"readonly\" | \"mode\">\n-\t\n\ncheckboxProps :{\nlabel : \"Text of Parent Label\"\n}\nsize\t\nthe size of the checkbox\n\"small\"\n\"large\"\n\"large\"\nsize\n\nsmall\n\nlarge\ndisabled\t\nboolean\n-\tSet boolean\nreadonly\t\nboolean\n-\tSet boolean\ntitleText\t\nAdditional titleText - if needed\nstring\n-\t\n\ntype\t\nit is either a standard type or a nested type, which means that the Checkbox Group has a parent element\n\"standard\"\n\"nested\"\n\"standard\"\ntype\n\nstandard\n\nnested\nsupportMessageProps\t\nthe support message of checkbox group\nODSSupportMessageProps\n-\tSet object\nvalue\t\nControlled: ids of the checked checkboxes\nstring[]\n-\tSet object\nonChildCheckboxChange\t\nChange handler for the Checkboxes\n((event: ODSCheckboxGroupChangeEvent) => void)\n-\t-\nGeneral\n\nCheckbox Group is a grouping of checkboxes. It enables users to toggle options on or off, providing a straightforward method for answering yes-no questions and selecting one or more options from multiple choices.\n\nBuilding on the simplicity of individual checkboxes, a checkbox group enables users to select multiple options from a list of choices. This component supports hierarchical structures, allowing primary options to expand into secondary lists of checkboxes, providing a flexible way to manage complex selections.\n\nWhen to use :\n\nUse the Checkbox Group to allow users to select one or more options from a list, like filtering items in a shop or choosing settings.\n\nNested: Options are grouped under a parent checkbox, making it ideal when many users are likely to select all options. Checkbox documentation\n\nWhen not to use :\n\nFor mutually exclusive choices, use the Radio Button Group.\n\nIf only one checkbox is needed, use the Checkbox component.\n\n\nAnatomy\n\n\nProperty Table\n\n\nUse Directives\n\nHow designers should use the component\n\nTypes\n\nDefault\n\nThe default variant is a group of checkboxes. Activating a checkbox does not affect other selections. It is considered to be selected when the control box has a checkmark.\n\n\nNested groups\n\nWhen the parent checkbox is checked, all child checkboxes are checked. If a parent checkbox is unchecked, all child checkboxes are unchecked.\n\n\nWhen some child checkboxes are selected, the parent checkbox shows an indeterminate state. Selecting the parent checkbox checks all child items, while deselecting it unchecks them all.\n\n\nSizes\n\nLarge and small\n\nThe Checkbox Group comes in two sizes, which should be chosen based on the size of the surrounding content. For Breakpoint S always use the small size.\n\n\nTitle and Labels\n\nTitle\n\nA title is optional and unnecessary if surrounding content already explains the checkbox group's purpose and details.\n\n\nLabels\n\nMake sure the user can quickly scan the labels of the checkbox.\n\n\nSupport Message\n\nAdditional context\n\nDisplay the Support Message component when additional context or user feedback is needed, such as for required checkbox groups.\n\n\nList items\n\nList container\n\nThe Checkbox Group's list container typically include 2-5 items. While 2-5 checkboxes are advised, more can be added if needed.\n\n\nBehaviours\n\nHow the component will behave in a live environment.\n\nSupport messages\n\nRequired input\n\nCheckbox groups can be optional or required. For required checkbox groups you can use the asterisk (*) in the Title.\n\n\nError Message\n\nWhen a selection in a required group is missing, show the error message. The message refers to the group and is shown below the list container.\n\n\nSelection states\n\nInteractive labels\n\nUsers are able to select either the text label or the checkbox to select an option.\n\n\nSelected, unselected & indeterminated\n\nThe parent checkbox has three states: selected, unselected and indeterminate. The child checkbox has two states: selected and unselected.\n\n\nNested groups\n\nParenting\n\nWhen the parent checkbox is checked, all child checkboxes are checked. If a parent checkbox is uncheced, all child checkboxes are unchecked.\n\n\nWhen some child checkboxes are selected, the parent checkbox shows an indeterminate state. Selecting the parent checkbox checks all child itmes, while deselecting it unchecks them all.\n\n\nDos and don'types\n\nIndeterminate\n\nThe indeterminate state is only for parent checkboxes in nested checkbox groups.\n\n\nGroup Support Message\n\nA support message should apply only to a checkbox group, as it refers to the entire group rather than individual checkboxes.\n\n\nComponent Variants\n\nStandard Large\n\n\nSupport Message Informative Large\n\n\nSupport Message Error Large\n\n\nStandard Small\n\n\nSupport Message Informative Small\n\n\nSupport Message Error Small\n\n\nColour Schemes\n\nHow it works (or is restricted) across colour schemes\n\nWhite\n\n\nBlack\n\n\nMagenta\n\nThis scheme is restricted. Checkbox Group component can only be used on neutral, white and black colour schemes.\n\n\nSecondary\n\nThis scheme is restricted. Checkbox Group component can only be used on neutral, white and black colour schemes.\n\n\nExamples\n\nWeb Desktop\n\n\nWeb Mobile\n\n\nAccessibility\n\nThis OneDS component is compliant with WCAG 2.2 AA Standards.\n\nKey considerations for keyboard interactions and screen readers are included. Additionally, all components meet requirements for the contrast ratios.\n\nDesign considerations\n\nA disabled checkbox must not have a support message, and its label should not convey any crucial information needed to understand the context.\n\nRefer to the AX annotation guide for detailed designer instructions on accessibility annotations.\n\nDevelopment considerations\n\nNo further development considerations required.\n\nWhile this individual component is accessible, building fully usable interfaces requires further attention. For guidance, refer to our OneExperience accessibility resources.\n\n", "code": [""], "stories": [{"id": "story--components-checkboxgroup--example", "html": "<div id=\"story--components-checkboxgroup--example-inner\" data-name=\"Example\" lang=\"en\"><div><div class=\"ODSColumn ODSCheckboxGroup ODSCheckboxGroup--size-large\" id=\"_r_1l_\"><div class=\"ODSColumn ODSCheckboxGroup-Title-Container\"><span class=\"ODSCheckboxGroup-Title\">Example Checkbox Group</span></div><div class=\"ODSColumn ODSCheckboxList--size-large\"><ul class=\"ODSColumn ODSCheckboxList--size-large-ListContainer\"><li class=\"ODSCheckboxGroup-ListItem\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSCheckbox ODSCheckbox--size-large ODSCheckbox--mode-standard ODSCheckbox--selected-selected\" id=\"example-1\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSCheckboxIcon ODSCheckboxIcon--size-large ODSCheckboxIcon--selected-selected\"><input aria-checked=\"true\" aria-disabled=\"false\" aria-readonly=\"false\" id=\"_r_1m_\" aria-invalid=\"false\" class=\"sr-only ODSCheckboxIcon-Input\" type=\"checkbox\" checked=\"\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSCheckboxIcon-Icon ODSCheckboxIcon-Icon--selected-selected ODSCheckboxIcon-Icon--size-large\"><svg class=\"ODSIcon ODSCheckboxIcon-Checkmark ODSCheckboxIcon-Checkmark--selected-selected\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><g fill=\"currentColor\"><g><path clip-rule=\"evenodd\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M20.884 5.616a1.25 1.25 0 0 1 0 1.768l-11 11a1.25 1.25 0 0 1-1.768 0l-5-5a1.25 1.25 0 0 1 1.768-1.768L9 15.732 19.116 5.616a1.25 1.25 0 0 1 1.768 0\"></path></g></g></svg></div></div><span class=\"ODSColumn ODSCheckbox-LabelMessage ODSCheckbox-LabelMessage--size-large\"><label class=\"ODSCheckbox-Label ODSCheckbox-Label--size-large ODSCheckbox-Label--mode-standard\" for=\"_r_1m_\">Option 1</label></span></div></li><li class=\"ODSCheckboxGroup-ListItem\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSCheckbox ODSCheckbox--size-large ODSCheckbox--mode-standard ODSCheckbox--selected-unselected\" id=\"example-2\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSCheckboxIcon ODSCheckboxIcon--size-large ODSCheckboxIcon--selected-unselected\"><input aria-checked=\"false\" aria-disabled=\"false\" aria-readonly=\"false\" id=\"_r_1n_\" aria-invalid=\"false\" class=\"sr-only ODSCheckboxIcon-Input\" type=\"checkbox\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSCheckboxIcon-Icon ODSCheckboxIcon-Icon--selected-unselected ODSCheckboxIcon-Icon--size-large\"></div></div><span class=\"ODSColumn ODSCheckbox-LabelMessage ODSCheckbox-LabelMessage--size-large\"><label class=\"ODSCheckbox-Label ODSCheckbox-Label--size-large ODSCheckbox-Label--mode-standard\" for=\"_r_1n_\">Option 2</label></span></div></li><li class=\"ODSCheckboxGroup-ListItem\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSCheckbox ODSCheckbox--size-large ODSCheckbox--mode-standard ODSCheckbox--selected-selected\" id=\"example-3\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSCheckboxIcon ODSCheckboxIcon--size-large ODSCheckboxIcon--selected-selected\"><input aria-checked=\"true\" aria-disabled=\"false\" aria-readonly=\"false\" id=\"_r_1o_\" aria-invalid=\"false\" class=\"sr-only ODSCheckboxIcon-Input\" type=\"checkbox\" checked=\"\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSCheckboxIcon-Icon ODSCheckboxIcon-Icon--selected-selected ODSCheckboxIcon-Icon--size-large\"><svg class=\"ODSIcon ODSCheckboxIcon-Checkmark ODSCheckboxIcon-Checkmark--selected-selected\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" 